      "question": {
        ":question/id": "129dd18f-6700-5ffb-9ca8-25a04326a78f",
        ":question/problem": "Use the substitution $u=4 x$. Which integral is obtained?\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|4 x|\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=4 x$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(4)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nWork on a connected real interval where $|4 x|>1$.\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}=\\frac{1}{4}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{1}{|4 x|\\sqrt{16 x^{2} - 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\left|{u}\\right|}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe transformed integral is\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\left|{u}\\right|}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "3db76bd0-786f-52f1-ae29-26420c6d4c60",
            ":answer-field/key": "answer",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
            ":answer-field/choices": [
              {
                ":answer/id": "f1b16480-9c36-50f9-807e-8bef4c87f22a",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{3}{4}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\left|{u}\\right|}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "9292dbeb-04c1-5a32-825d-48db9072d490",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\left|{u}\\right|}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)"
              },
              {
                ":answer/id": "b38d76bb-3a13-5edd-b277-e294d22f2520",
                ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
                ":answer/value": "\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u^{2} - 1} \\left|{u}\\right|}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)"
              },
